				<r3d:description language="eng">The Oxford Text Archive develops, collects, catalogues and preserves electronic literary and linguistic resources for use in Higher Education, in research, teaching and learning. We also give advice on the creation and use of these resources, and are involved in the development of standards and infrastructure for electronic language resources. The Oxford Text Archive is a national repository, part of the Infrastructure for DIgital Arts and Humanities Programme of the Arts and Humanties Research Council, and the national repository for the CLARIN European research infrastructure in the UK.</r3d:description>
